; Installer hooks — where the speech model goes, and why it is not a resource.
;
; This is a TEMPLATE. `crates/ov-app/build.rs` fills in the placeholder in
; NSIS_HOOK_POSTINSTALL below and writes the real `installer-hooks.nsh` beside
; it, which tauri.conf.json points at. Do not edit the generated file; edit this
; one. (The placeholder token is deliberately not repeated in this comment: it
; is substituted by plain string replacement, and an earlier version of this
; file named it here — so the first substitution landed in the comment and NSIS
; met an IfFileExists at top level.)
;
; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
; Why the model is installed here rather than bundled as a Tauri resource
;
; The 631 MB Parakeet model ships inside the installer so a fresh install can
; dictate immediately, offline, with no first-run download. The obvious way to do
; that is `bundle.resources` in tauri.conf.json. That way is wrong here.
;
; The original reason given here was that this keeps the model out of the updater
; payload. It does not, and building it is what showed that: `File` embeds the
; weights into the installer executable, and the updater artifact is a zip of
; that same executable. An update carries the model whichever mechanism puts it
; there. That claim is corrected in ADR 0008 rather than quietly deleted.
;
; The reason that survives is placement. This installs the model beside the
; application, where NSIS_HOOK_POSTUNINSTALL below reclaims it on uninstall,
; rather than inside Tauri's resource tree.
;
; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
; Why this is generated rather than written by hand
;
; NSIS `!ifdef` tests an NSIS *define*, and Tauri does not forward environment
; variables into the generated script as defines. An earlier version of this file
; guarded the copy with `!ifdef MODEL_SOURCE_DIR` and passed MODEL_SOURCE_DIR as
; an environment variable. The guard was never true. The build succeeded, printed
; no warning, and produced a 9 MB installer with no speech model in it — which
; would have looked entirely fine until the first person tried to dictate.
;
; So the file paths are baked in at build time, where their absence is visible.
; When no model is present the substitution is empty and the installer builds
; without one: a developer packaging locally should not be forced into a 482 MB
; download they did not ask for, and release.yml asserts the model exists before
; it ever invokes `tauri build`.

!macro NSIS_HOOK_PREINSTALL
!macroend

!macro NSIS_HOOK_POSTINSTALL
@MODEL_FILES@
!macroend

!macro NSIS_HOOK_PREUNINSTALL
!macroend

!macro NSIS_HOOK_POSTUNINSTALL
  ; Uninstalling must not strand 631 MB. The weights are ours, they live inside
  ; $INSTDIR, and nothing else on the machine refers to them.
  RMDir /r "$INSTDIR\models"
!macroend
